# Start with current evidence

1. Read `memory-bank/.now.md`.
2. Read `memory-bank/00-start-here.md` and only the task-relevant memory files.
3. Check `git status`, branch, HEAD and runtime. Preserve all pre-existing changes.
4. Treat code and verified runtime evidence as truth; correct docs when they differ.

Avoid reading `.venv/`, `.env`, `profile/`, `out/*.png`, `out/form_map*.json`, and sample images unless a task requires them. Do not print secrets or personal data. Do not rerun already-established OCR samples without changing extraction code or needing new evidence.

After a meaningful change, run relevant verification, update `memory-bank/.now.md`, update stable technical knowledge in the relevant memory file, and selectively commit only your own bounded changes.

## Keep test artifacts bounded

Do not allow temporary test logs, stdout/stderr, scratch files, or repeated validation outputs to accumulate in Git. Keep them in a temporary directory or ignored local location during execution. Preserve a compact reproducible record (check source, pinned inputs, result/report, and hashes); retain raw output while failures are under diagnosis, then prune it after disposition. For completed post-patch-validation runs, use `scripts/dev/prune-validation-logs.py` and inspect its dry run before applying. Never bulk-delete a validation directory or user files.
